Here are the ways to copy-paste in Kali Linux terminal:\
Method 1 â€ƒ´ Easiest (Right-click paste)\
\
    Copy the script from here â€ƒ´ select text âƒ¦ƒ² Ctrl+C on your keyboard\
    Open terminal in Kali\
    Type nano script1_system_identity.sh\
    Right-click inside the terminal âƒ¦ƒ² click Paste\
    Ctrl+O to save âƒ¦ƒ² Enter âƒ¦ƒ² Ctrl+X to exit\
\
Method 2 â€ƒ´ Keyboard shortcut\
\
In Kali terminal, the shortcuts are different from normal:\
Action	Normal	Kali Terminal\
Copy	Ctrl+C	Ctrl+Shift+C\
Paste	Ctrl+V	Ctrl+Shift+V\
\
    âƒºƒ€ï¸ƒ¯ Ctrl+C in terminal means cancel/stop a program, not copy â€ƒ´ so always use Ctrl+Shift+V to paste.\
\
Method 3 â€ƒ´ If you're on a VM\
\
If Kali is running inside VirtualBox or VMware on your Windows PC:\
\
    Copy the script text on Windows âƒ¦ƒ² Ctrl+C\
    Click inside the Kali VM window\
    Right-click âƒ¦ƒ² Paste or Ctrl+Shift+V\
\
    If paste doesn't work in a VM, you may need to install Guest Additions (VirtualBox) or VMware Tools â€ƒ´ let me know if that's the case.\
